-- Baseline, part 2 of 2: what the site adds to Supabase's own schemas.
--
-- What: generated from production on 2026-10-20, after 0116_security_fixes_followup was
-- applied, by supabase/tools/dump-platform-objects.sql. It holds the storage buckets
-- (idempotent upserts), the storage.objects policies, the handle_new_user function with its
-- on_auth_user_created trigger on auth.users, and the default privileges in `public`. Below
-- this header the output is unchanged, except the wording of the commented-out lines at the end.
--
-- Why: `supabase db dump` covers only the site's own schemas (part 1,
-- 20261020120000_baseline_schema.sql). Without this part a rebuilt database would have no
-- buckets, no storage policies and no profile row for new sign-ups. It runs after part 1
-- because the policies and the trigger function use the site's tables and functions.
-- Its ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES lines also switch back on the defaults part 1 switched off
-- while the site's objects were created.
--
-- The supabase_admin default privileges at the end stay commented out: they cannot be set
-- as the migration role, and a new Supabase project already has them.
--
-- Never edit this file. Change these objects with a new timestamped migration and its down script.

-- Generated by supabase/tools/dump-platform-objects.sql
